
The originally internal file 'FAMEInternSetStructs.h' of FAME is now
public with FAME.library 6.0 and with FAME 2.0 and is called now
'FAMESetStructs.h'. 

In 'FAMESetStructs.h' you will find all the structures for accessing
to FAME config/settings files.

But *PLEASE* do not use them now direclty with DOS functions to read and
modify files like you want of FAME on disk. It was internal all the time
to keep people away from the FAME settings while there is no better solution.
Now with FAME.library 6.0 we have the better solution and because of this
the structures are given free... for use with the FAME Config Feature!

Only access those files directly in a few cases where it's really impossible
to do it via using FAME Config Feature.

<EOF>
